['What does PikoBuy say happens after an item reaches the warehouse?','Its beginner guide describes check-in, photo confirmation and a defect check. The forwarding terms add that specialist inspection is not available for every special or professional product, so warehouse photos are evidence for visible points rather than a product guarantee.'],
['Can QC photos prove authenticity, fit or long-term quality?','No. PikoBuy describes a warehouse inspection and photos; its terms also say it is not the manufacturer and generally not the seller of record. Photos can help compare the visible item, but they cannot prove origin, fit, material performance or future durability.'],
['When can a return request be made?','PikoBuy’s returns page says that an eligible request can be submitted within five days after the status becomes “In Warehouse,” counted as 120 hours from the following hour. Eligibility, resale condition and the seller’s rules still matter, and applications after the window may not be accepted.'],
['Who pays when an eligible item is returned for a personal reason?','The published policy lists the return shipping, the seller’s original domestic shipping and a RMB 5 service fee for an unconditional return. It also says the seller must consent to the return, so buyers should check the live order and seller response before treating any refund as certain.'],
['Is international delivery guaranteed once a parcel is submitted?','No. PikoBuy says routes differ in delivery time and billing method. Its Shipping Terms state that parcels use third-party logistics providers and that customs, damage, loss and peak-season delays are risks the customer must assess and bear.'],
['What should be checked before the first payment?','Confirm the live listing, exact color, size and quantity. PikoBuy’s guide says the actual purchase price can differ and an out-of-stock order is refunded. Its Terms also place taxes, duties, brokerage and similar cross-border charges on the user where they apply.']
